WEBVTT

00:01:38.960 --> 00:01:42.220
Do you seriously want this car?

00:01:42.220 --> 00:01:43.410
Yeah.

00:01:43.410 --> 00:01:45.600
I understood after sitting next to you,

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:48.990
from your driving style and that you know this car so well.

00:01:48.990 --> 00:01:51.850
The driving style hasn't changed.

00:01:51.850 --> 00:01:54.260
You did well maintaining this car as it was.

00:01:58.590 --> 00:02:00.170
Can I ask you a question?

00:02:00.170 --> 00:02:01.350
Sure.

00:02:01.350 --> 00:02:05.190
What do you intend to do with this FC after acquiring it?

00:02:05.190 --> 00:02:07.690
Do you want to drive it just because it's nostalgic,

00:02:07.690 --> 00:02:10.870
or do you just want to remember the past.

00:02:10.870 --> 00:02:12.190
Is it something like that?

00:02:13.830 --> 00:02:16.400
Time has stopped...

00:02:17.530 --> 00:02:19.410
You're sure saying some complicated things.

00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:24.830
Since Zero closed down, I've been
separated all these five years from FC.

00:02:24.830 --> 00:02:29.420
I got a good job as a car commentator
and made pretty good money.

00:02:30.660 --> 00:02:34.170
Although I shouldn't have any dissatisfactions by now, but somehow...

00:02:36.170 --> 00:02:39.880
It felt that as if time has stalled.

00:02:53.420 --> 00:02:57.970
<i>Thoughts That Won't Stop</i>

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:04.220
It sure is good. The rotary is the best.

00:03:04.220 --> 00:03:07.070
The car is really fast, right?

00:03:07.070 --> 00:03:09.920
Yeah, this guy didn't change.

00:03:09.920 --> 00:03:15.230
But, in order to fight with Z, there is
something more that I need to add on.

00:03:15.230 --> 00:03:17.160
Z will also be tuned by RGO.

00:03:17.750 --> 00:03:18.920
Is Ohta-san going to do it?

00:03:19.420 --> 00:03:22.920
No, I asked his daughter, Rikako-san.

00:03:22.920 --> 00:03:26.310
His daughter? I see.

00:03:26.310 --> 00:03:28.140
This sounds fun.

00:03:28.140 --> 00:03:30.090
It'll be a match when we meet next time.

00:03:30.950 --> 00:03:31.890
Yes.

00:03:37.420 --> 00:03:39.860
I don't have any conditions, it's up to you.

00:03:43.940 --> 00:03:44.860
I'll try.

00:04:02.700 --> 00:04:04.640
Hello, sorry to disturb you.

00:04:05.460 --> 00:04:06.230
Good day.

00:04:06.230 --> 00:04:09.440
Shima-san and uncle Kitami! What's the matter?

00:04:11.020 --> 00:04:13.540
If you'd like, I'm here to give you advice.

00:04:14.250 --> 00:04:17.650
I heard Akio asked you to overhaul this car.

00:04:17.650 --> 00:04:22.870
Please do so. I had wanted to ask you, about the secret of this Z.

00:04:23.290 --> 00:04:24.370
Secret?

00:04:25.510 --> 00:04:28.370
Such as are there any extremely special parts installed?

00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:31.500
And also how you manufactured and assembled them.

00:04:32.640 --> 00:04:35.740
I'm sorry so say this, but there's no special parts at all.

00:04:35.740 --> 00:04:38.720
The cam and piston are all normal L-Type parts.

00:04:39.110 --> 00:04:39.960
Really?

00:04:39.960 --> 00:04:43.330
Yeah, the turbine is also an old TD...

00:04:43.330 --> 00:04:47.900
It can't be said to be effective in the current
times where ball bearings are mainstream.

00:04:47.900 --> 00:04:51.860
Just normal parts being assembled in a normal fashion.

00:04:51.860 --> 00:04:53.970
There is no secret at all.

00:04:55.580 --> 00:04:56.210
But...

00:04:56.210 --> 00:04:56.970
But?

00:04:56.970 --> 00:04:59.760
There is only one special part.

00:04:59.760 --> 00:05:01.950
It's he only part I've never touched.

00:05:05.740 --> 00:05:07.250
It's the crankshaft.

00:05:07.250 --> 00:05:08.450
Crank?

00:05:08.450 --> 00:05:13.110
It's not a full counter forge, super high class one...

00:05:13.110 --> 00:05:16.810
It's just a rather normal crank for 3.0s and 3.1s.

00:05:18.190 --> 00:05:22.700
But, even now I cannot forget that
stable feeling when I took hold of it.

00:05:22.700 --> 00:05:25.560
This is the only part that can't be meddled with.

00:05:25.560 --> 00:05:29.250
Whoever gets their hands on this, will think so too.

00:05:29.920 --> 00:05:30.980
That is...

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:36.940
We really cannot meddle with it, no matter what?

00:05:41.030 --> 00:05:46.000
Of course it's up to you, because you're
the one who was requested by the owner.

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:47.450
You can do everything as you like.

00:05:47.920 --> 00:05:48.950
I understand.

00:05:50.430 --> 00:05:52.360
We have another thing to look forward to now.

00:05:56.250 --> 00:06:00.610
It's rare for you to call me over at this hour, Akio-kun.

00:06:01.590 --> 00:06:04.970
Yeah, since it won't be as suspicious as being alone.

00:06:05.320 --> 00:06:07.210
Won't be suspicious?

00:06:09.100 --> 00:06:11.290
Eh, why a book store?!

00:06:11.290 --> 00:06:13.640
Kijima-san taught me this.

00:06:14.460 --> 00:06:19.140
If I read a book alone at the book store,
I'll be suspected as a shoplifter.

00:06:24.330 --> 00:06:27.650
13B Turbo. Is this the FC's one?

00:06:28.820 --> 00:06:32.220
For a rotary, the engine is really compact.

00:06:32.220 --> 00:06:34.580
With that, it can go over 300km/h.

00:06:34.580 --> 00:06:37.660
I understand now after reading this book. I misunderstood before.

00:06:37.660 --> 00:06:41.120
I thought rotary cars were all just handling machines.

00:06:41.780 --> 00:06:46.390
Or stuff like well-balanced packages, or 50-50 weight distributions.

00:06:48.380 --> 00:06:53.380
But I was wrong. Rotary cars are high power machines.

00:06:54.300 --> 00:06:56.470
I didn't knew anything at all.

00:07:00.300 --> 00:07:02.650
Akio-kun, there's something written about it here too!

00:07:09.110 --> 00:07:13.110
<i>There is only one special part. It's the crankshaft.</i>

00:07:22.200 --> 00:07:25.050
<i>This is the only part that can't be meddled with.</i>

00:07:25.310 --> 00:07:27.650
<i>Whoever gets their hands on this, will think so too.</i>

00:07:38.610 --> 00:07:40.840
<i>Seems like Z is going to run again.</i>

00:07:50.220 --> 00:07:52.770
<i>After I won the battle at Ooi's straight road,</i>

00:07:52.770 --> 00:07:55.110
<i>I heard that Z will be running once again,</i>

00:07:55.110 --> 00:07:57.700
<i>and I should have been excited that...</i>

00:07:57.700 --> 00:08:01.700
<i>I can experience that moment again. But why...</i>

00:08:05.210 --> 00:08:07.710
<i>Why are my feelings so mixed up?</i>

00:08:09.710 --> 00:08:11.720
<i>Haven't I been looking for it?</i>

00:08:12.120 --> 00:08:14.420
<i>The battle tactics that will shorten my life?</i>

00:08:37.540 --> 00:08:38.480
Yes, hello?

00:08:39.460 --> 00:08:42.960
Yeah, it's me. What happened, calling me at this hour?

00:08:42.960 --> 00:08:46.950
An accident? You? Alright, I'll be there right away!

00:08:46.950 --> 00:08:48.310
Thank you.

00:08:50.950 --> 00:08:55.460
<i>With just a speed of less than 50km/h,
what in the world was I doing?</i>

00:08:56.430 --> 00:08:58.860
<i>Why I my heart so confused until this extent?</i>

00:09:05.470 --> 00:09:09.240
<i>There's really no secrets in this engine.</i>

00:09:10.450 --> 00:09:12.110
How long do you intend to keep staring at that?

00:09:14.030 --> 00:09:19.870
No matter how great it is, in the end it's
still a L-Type SOHC 2 valve engine, right?

00:09:19.870 --> 00:09:21.740
That's true, but...

00:09:21.740 --> 00:09:26.430
I can't wait to see it, not a Kitami-tuned one, but your own L-type.

00:09:27.400 --> 00:09:30.470
This L-type that you're assembling, is going to be installed in Z.

00:09:30.470 --> 00:09:34.070
What kind of sounds it'll make, and how it will run.

00:09:35.250 --> 00:09:38.960
Besides tuning machines are a never-ending
quest of finding their weaknesses.

00:09:40.510 --> 00:09:44.520
If we try to improve the good parts,
absolutely nothing will happen, right?

00:09:45.210 --> 00:09:48.760
For human beings, if we find their good
points and praise them, they may improve,

00:09:48.760 --> 00:09:50.520
but the machines are not like that.

00:09:50.520 --> 00:09:57.530
So, if you get lost, the only way is to find the weak points,
and try to solve the problems, carefully one by one.

00:09:57.530 --> 00:10:01.110
There is no magic for tuning, you get that.

00:10:02.000 --> 00:10:05.700
If the power is increased, defects will definitely appear.

00:10:05.700 --> 00:10:08.210
You then just have to eliminate them one by one.

00:10:08.860 --> 00:10:11.720
And one day, it will become an extraordinary tuning.

00:10:13.710 --> 00:10:15.220
That's how it is.

00:10:24.320 --> 00:10:29.400
<i>Good. I'll still step further.</i>

00:10:37.150 --> 00:10:38.740
<i>If anything were to happen to me,</i>

00:10:38.740 --> 00:10:42.860
<i>whatever I have amassed until today will be lost,</i>

00:10:42.860 --> 00:10:44.580
<i>including my money and my job...</i>

00:10:46.910 --> 00:10:48.580
<i>What other things do I have?!</i>

00:10:51.790 --> 00:10:55.800
Just a bit more... wait for me, Z, BlackBird!

00:11:18.490 --> 00:11:22.230
<i>What kind of image you see when you're
building it, that is what's important, right?</i>

00:11:23.420 --> 00:11:26.010
<i>How far can you realize your ideals?</i>

00:11:26.010 --> 00:11:29.550
<i>I'll always be watching you from Osaka.</i>

00:11:35.220 --> 00:11:39.390
<i>They're all normal parts, there's no special parts at all.</i>

00:11:40.580 --> 00:11:42.970
<i>No matter how high level we assembled it,</i>

00:11:42.970 --> 00:11:45.590
<i>it doesn't necessary mean that something
will be changed significantly.</i>

00:11:47.390 --> 00:11:52.140
<i>But even though every single part holds no secret,</i>

00:11:52.140 --> 00:11:56.660
<i>once the engine is assembled and installed inside Z,</i>

00:11:57.270 --> 00:12:00.860
<i>for sure something will change, something new will be born.</i>

00:12:19.010 --> 00:12:19.750
How was it?

00:12:20.850 --> 00:12:22.760
Well, it was something.

00:12:30.250 --> 00:12:31.720
When did you finished?

00:12:32.570 --> 00:12:33.820
Just a while ago.

00:12:33.820 --> 00:12:35.480
It seems to move well.

00:12:36.930 --> 00:12:40.190
Uncle Kitami, if you don't mind, please come with me for a while.

00:12:40.670 --> 00:12:42.620
I want to run it at around 100km/h.

00:12:42.620 --> 00:12:47.460
A warm-up run? Warming up is a privilege
for owners, right? Akio will be angry.

00:12:48.150 --> 00:12:50.310
It's not warming up but wrapping up.

00:12:50.310 --> 00:12:52.220
I just want to make sure it's fully ready.

00:12:52.220 --> 00:12:54.450
Those are the rights of tuners, right?

00:12:55.680 --> 00:12:56.670
Alright.

00:13:05.820 --> 00:13:10.430
As might has been expected, you
are able to maintain 3000rpm nicely,

00:13:10.430 --> 00:13:12.240
and without initiating boost.

00:13:12.240 --> 00:13:16.270
Since we did drive and tweak it thoroughly, for this L-Type system.

00:13:19.430 --> 00:13:20.810
Did you find out anything?

00:13:22.190 --> 00:13:24.600
That there was no secret.

00:13:24.600 --> 00:13:28.830
The engine block, piston and cam too, are all normal.

00:13:29.390 --> 00:13:33.860
But the crankshaft is different after all.

00:13:33.860 --> 00:13:38.330
Even though it's a L28 Custom 3.1 liter, but the stroke is 84mm.

00:13:39.130 --> 00:13:43.000
The stroke is set 1mm longer than normal 3.1 liter engines.

00:13:44.530 --> 00:13:48.360
The additional displacement value achieved is only 38cc,

00:13:48.360 --> 00:13:51.090
which is a little more than 1% of the total displacement.

00:13:51.570 --> 00:13:58.450
For a normal L28 Custom 3.1 liter engine, with the inner
diameter of 89mm multiplied by the stroke of 83mm,

00:13:58.450 --> 00:14:02.180
the total displacement is a 3096cc 3.1 engine.

00:14:02.730 --> 00:14:05.110
This is the most well-balanced L-Type.

00:14:07.620 --> 00:14:11.640
However, this Z has a stroke of 84mm, which is 1mm longer.

00:14:11.640 --> 00:14:17.490
89mm multiplied by 84mm, you get a 3134cc
3.1 specification that breaks the balance.

00:14:18.350 --> 00:14:20.630
Why is such an unreasonable increase of displacement done?

00:14:21.290 --> 00:14:24.630
That's right. You're pretty sharp.

00:14:26.580 --> 00:14:31.260
If there exists a mechanical secret in
the Z, it's only that 1mm longer stroke,

00:14:32.110 --> 00:14:36.090
and that 1% more of increased displacement.

00:14:38.110 --> 00:14:41.720
My tuning life which started from L-Types,

00:14:41.720 --> 00:14:44.820
in the end I couldn't escape from the borders of L-Types.

00:14:46.450 --> 00:14:53.140
But I'm proud of this tuner's life of mine, where I understood
L-types more than anybody else and lived alongside it.

00:14:54.080 --> 00:14:58.590
However, I'm not going to touch L-Types in my life anymore.

00:14:59.760 --> 00:15:01.340
After this, it all depends on you,

00:15:02.010 --> 00:15:05.340
whether you let this Z continue to run as it is now,

00:15:05.340 --> 00:15:08.840
or complete it as the ultimate L28 Custom Twin Turbo.

00:15:13.280 --> 00:15:14.550
Kitami-san did?

00:15:16.590 --> 00:15:19.060
He said, "I'm not going to touch L-Types in my life anymore."

00:15:21.970 --> 00:15:24.410
Can you do a warm-up run for 500km?

00:15:24.410 --> 00:15:28.320
After that I'll check it once more and then go full out.

00:15:28.740 --> 00:15:29.490
Got it.

00:15:32.960 --> 00:15:38.240
<i>I replaced the piston rod and crankshaft's metal, and for the head the valve guide is replaced,</i>

00:15:38.240 --> 00:15:41.250
<i>and some sealing-related gaskets.</i>

00:15:41.870 --> 00:15:45.720
<i>They're only normal consumer items.</i>

00:15:47.230 --> 00:15:50.690
<i>It's quite a normal overhaul and assembly.</i>

00:15:50.690 --> 00:15:52.660
<i>That's why, there's no change in power.</i>

00:15:52.660 --> 00:15:55.980
<i>Something like a refresh, like it's new, that's all.</i>

00:15:58.730 --> 00:16:02.810
<i>It's not been tuned, so nothing has been changed.</i>

00:16:08.880 --> 00:16:10.390
Good morning! You're early.

00:16:11.870 --> 00:16:14.260
Could it be, you did the warm-up until morning?

00:16:14.260 --> 00:16:17.420
Yes. For the time being, I drove 800km.

00:16:18.530 --> 00:16:19.930
Not bad.

00:16:19.930 --> 00:16:23.170
So, how was it? Did you hit 300km/h?

00:16:23.170 --> 00:16:27.660
No, I tried not to go above 4000rpm.

00:16:27.660 --> 00:16:30.870
Why not?

00:16:30.870 --> 00:16:34.890
She only re-assembled and the parts
have not been changed much, right?

00:16:34.890 --> 00:16:37.690
If you drive around 100km/h, you can still go all out, right?

00:16:38.460 --> 00:16:43.440
Yes, that's true, but somehow that feels like a waste.

00:16:44.890 --> 00:16:47.650
What's up with this?

00:16:48.580 --> 00:16:53.090
He came early in the morning and
left it here, saying he drove 800km.

00:16:53.090 --> 00:16:56.400
So, just check the whole thing, change the
oil and pass it back to him at once, alright?

00:16:57.960 --> 00:17:00.090
Seems like he really does like to drive.

00:17:00.090 --> 00:17:01.740
Did he say anything else?

00:17:01.740 --> 00:17:03.500
He doesn't want to waste it.

00:17:04.970 --> 00:17:07.410
A sense to not speed recklessly.

00:17:08.350 --> 00:17:11.370
That's right, Eiji also said the same thing.

00:17:12.250 --> 00:17:14.940
<i>There's a sense of quality driving in your engine.</i>

00:17:16.310 --> 00:17:19.670
A person who understands will be able to see it.

00:17:22.770 --> 00:17:25.930
It appears to be visible damage only on the left side,

00:17:25.930 --> 00:17:28.750
but there's a slight warp on the right pillar section.

00:17:29.560 --> 00:17:32.080
It wasn't even moving at more than 50km/h, right?

00:17:32.080 --> 00:17:34.940
Just because of that, the whole body was warped?

00:17:34.940 --> 00:17:37.970
It's more than enough, even below 50km/h,

00:17:37.970 --> 00:17:41.820
depending on the angle and which part
was hit, it can be seriously warped.

00:17:42.420 --> 00:17:45.040
This is difficult to repair.

00:17:45.750 --> 00:17:48.290
Takagi, you look happy.

00:17:49.260 --> 00:17:50.200
No, not really...

00:17:51.750 --> 00:17:53.510
Can't you do something about it?

00:17:54.520 --> 00:17:57.010
There are many ways to just cover it up.

00:17:57.010 --> 00:18:00.780
For example, by completely replacing the power train.

00:18:00.780 --> 00:18:05.480
Convert the current 964 Turbo's power train to a 993's body?

00:18:05.480 --> 00:18:09.760
That's right. Your preference for 2WD is maintained.

00:18:09.760 --> 00:18:11.950
That's definitely a good choice,

00:18:11.950 --> 00:18:16.990
but I don't think that's Takagi-san's...
no, both of your real intentions.

00:18:18.490 --> 00:18:19.850
What do you mean?

00:18:19.850 --> 00:18:25.540
For example, remain monocoque only at the

00:18:25.540 --> 00:18:28.830
And also make all outer parts with carbon fiber.

00:18:28.830 --> 00:18:30.830
Carbon?

00:18:31.750 --> 00:18:35.870
I saw a car like this in an American technical book before.

00:18:36.680 --> 00:18:40.950
If this car is 700hp and the car wight is 1500kg,

00:18:40.950 --> 00:18:43.880
then the power-to-weight ratio is about 2.15kg per hp.

00:18:44.510 --> 00:18:49.470
If we can reduce the weight by another 200kg,
the power-to-weight ratio will then fall into the 1.x range.

00:18:49.470 --> 00:18:51.170
That's right.

00:18:51.170 --> 00:18:53.670
Its movement will be that of a completely different car.

00:18:53.670 --> 00:18:56.070
It will, without a doubt.

00:18:56.070 --> 00:18:57.840
But what about the car safety inspection?

00:18:57.840 --> 00:19:00.780
Since we're cutting a monocoque body and installing carbon panels,

00:19:00.780 --> 00:19:02.690
either way we still have to file an application for the modifications.

00:19:02.690 --> 00:19:05.950
No problem. I have a year more until the car safety inspection.

00:19:05.950 --> 00:19:08.960
In other words, you will scrap this car within a year?

00:19:08.960 --> 00:19:11.460
It'll be impossible if I wasn't mentally prepared for it.

00:19:12.110 --> 00:19:14.650
That car will regain its speed.

00:19:14.650 --> 00:19:17.460
No matter what, since it has already started to run.

00:19:17.460 --> 00:19:18.800
Because of Z?

00:19:19.670 --> 00:19:24.720
But a patched up monocoque might not be able to run straight.

00:19:24.720 --> 00:19:27.230
I'll make it run straight.

00:19:28.630 --> 00:19:29.810
How about Kitami-san?

00:19:29.810 --> 00:19:34.970
No problem for me, as long as you can
prepare some money for fixing up the engine.

00:19:34.970 --> 00:19:36.650
Then, that's decided already.

00:19:36.650 --> 00:19:38.230
Yes, it is.

00:19:40.770 --> 00:19:44.460
Actually, it's because of this accident that
I could understand something only now.

00:19:45.160 --> 00:19:48.280
There's only one person chosen by that Z.

00:19:49.140 --> 00:19:50.650
I've been chasing after that Z all this time.

00:19:51.490 --> 00:19:55.810
When we meet, I'm able to immediately
jump into action. That was my instinct.

00:19:56.480 --> 00:19:58.710
But actually, I wanted to be chosen.

00:19:59.860 --> 00:20:03.420
After I realized that fact once more, I was astonished.

00:20:04.570 --> 00:20:06.850
Having resonated with something in Z,

00:20:06.850 --> 00:20:09.240
it's impossible to just forget about it or separate from it.

00:20:09.830 --> 00:20:11.510
There are only two choices.

00:20:12.660 --> 00:20:16.190
Either being beside it or facing it head on.

00:20:24.750 --> 00:20:26.180
You just got off work?

00:20:28.840 --> 00:20:29.450
Here.

00:20:29.800 --> 00:20:30.590
What's this?

00:20:32.490 --> 00:20:34.420
I left the car at the garage.

00:20:36.200 --> 00:20:40.840
This receipt is like a child's scribble, right? And isn't it too cheap?

00:20:41.360 --> 00:20:45.970
Since Rikako Speed Factory is an honest shop, it's alright.

00:20:46.710 --> 00:20:50.970
The cost for the parts are written in the
RGO's order form without permission.

00:20:50.970 --> 00:20:54.570
That means it's free of charge, but there's profit too.

00:20:54.570 --> 00:20:55.980
Is that fine?

00:20:55.980 --> 00:20:57.410
It's fine!

00:20:57.410 --> 00:21:00.040
I wanted to do it even though there's no pay.

00:21:00.040 --> 00:21:02.820
And I changed some stuff a bit.

00:21:04.190 --> 00:21:05.090
Which part?

00:21:05.090 --> 00:21:07.380
I changed the oil circulation system.

00:21:07.380 --> 00:21:10.330
Oil... so, what's the difference now?

00:21:10.330 --> 00:21:14.330
The oil pressure will be more stable, and
the center of gravity will be a little lower.

00:21:14.330 --> 00:21:15.650
Center of gravity...

00:21:19.360 --> 00:21:21.830
Did you know, BlackBird got into an accident?

00:21:22.340 --> 00:21:23.850
BlackBird did?

00:21:24.770 --> 00:21:28.330
It was a light accident but it caused
an unexpected amount of damage.

00:21:28.330 --> 00:21:32.710
And since it's going to be repaired, I heard that
its weight will be reduced and its body rebuilt,

00:21:33.450 --> 00:21:35.060
as well as engine reassembled.

00:21:36.730 --> 00:21:40.340
How is it, tough? Do you want to upgrade to a larger turbine?

00:21:40.340 --> 00:21:42.110
It's alright, you don't have to.

00:21:43.570 --> 00:21:46.900
I feel that after it's overhauled, it became much better, really.

00:21:46.900 --> 00:21:52.080
It's definitely not the same as before,
but it undoubtedly gained something new.

00:21:52.880 --> 00:21:56.550
If there's something required to be
done after this, that'll be actual driving.

00:22:00.550 --> 00:22:04.310
Whether it's a miracle or a will,

00:22:05.170 --> 00:22:08.090
if this guy really has something like this,

00:22:09.020 --> 00:22:13.600
the thing it lost will surely return. That's what I believe.

00:22:19.100 --> 00:22:24.640
<i>I see, after the oil circulation system was
changed, the center of gravity has been lowered.</i>

00:22:24.640 --> 00:22:27.140
<i>3rd gear, 8000rpm.</i>

00:22:27.150 --> 00:22:28.140
<i>4th gear.</i>

00:22:30.620 --> 00:22:33.120
<i>4th gear, 6000rpm.</i>

00:22:35.260 --> 00:22:37.510
<i>7000... 7500.</i>

00:22:38.580 --> 00:22:42.120
<i>A direct drive which conveys much more power.</i>

00:22:42.120 --> 00:22:44.250
<i>Direct rev to 8000rpm.</i>

00:22:45.630 --> 00:22:46.880
<i>Alright, shift to 5th gear!</i>

00:22:52.800 --> 00:22:54.810
<i>5th gear, 6000rpm.</i>

00:22:54.810 --> 00:22:57.300
<i>6500, 6700...</i>

00:22:57.880 --> 00:23:00.510
<i>6900, 7000!</i>

00:23:03.530 --> 00:23:08.170
<i>It can still go up! If I carefully increase the rev, at 5th gear overdrive,</i>

00:23:08.170 --> 00:23:10.990
<i>I can achieve a longer acceleration continuously!</i>

00:23:12.020 --> 00:23:14.030
<i>I can fight, once again!</i>
